{
  "__doc": "JOURNEY CONTRAST declarations for GET /api/ledger/journey (brief P0-3). This file exists for ONE reason: the screen must say 「본딩 · 압력」 where the ledger says `processed_with·params_actual.pressure_MPa`, and a Korean name for a step or a payload leaf is operator knowledge that the data does not carry. 🔴 IT IS NOT AN ITEM LIST. Nothing here decides what is COMPARED -- every leaf of every atom of the two marked subjects is compared whether it is named here or not, and an unnamed leaf renders as its RAW PATH (정직 우선, orchard rule). 🔴 BUT THE TWO HALVES OF THIS FILE FAIL DIFFERENTLY, so do not read the line above as 'delete it all and only the Korean is lost' -- an earlier version of this comment said exactly that and it was wrong. The three LABEL blocks (step_labels / family_labels / field_labels) narrow nothing: delete them and every segment, item and value is still produced, with raw paths in place of names. The `segments` block is STRUCTURAL: it is the only thing that says which predicate carries a journey and where the step name lives inside its payload, so deleting it leaves no axis to draw and GET /api/ledger/journey answers state='absent', reason='no_journey_predicate_declared', segments=[] -- a degraded ANSWER rather than an error, but an empty screen all the same.",
  "version": 1,

  "segments": {
    "__doc": "🔴 THE ONE STRUCTURAL DECLARATION, and it is the thing the P0-3 brief did NOT anticipate (the brief says 「새 선언 0개」 for data and 「라벨 선언 한 층」 for names). Segmenting a journey needs to know WHICH predicate carries a process step and WHERE inside its payload the step's name and family live. `server/ledger/vocabulary.py` declares that `processed_with`'s object requires ['step','step_family','eqp','recipe'] but nothing says which of those four IS the step -- reading it off position in that list would be a convention, and a convention is exactly what breaks the day a schema differs. So it is declared here. Adding a second journey-bearing predicate is an entry in this block and costs no Python. | `name_path` and `family_path` are dotted paths into `object_payload`. `family_path` may be omitted; the family then reads as 「미선언」 rather than being guessed from the step name.",
    "processed_with": {
      "family_path": "step_family",
      "name_path": "step"
    }
  },

  "family_labels": {
    "__doc": "step_family value -> Korean. An undeclared family renders as its raw value.",
    "fab": "전공정",
    "packaging": "후공정",
    "metrology": "계측"
  },

  "step_labels": {
    "__doc": "step value -> Korean. This is where 「본딩」 comes from and it is the reason `SYN-BD-03` is no longer the only thing on the row. An undeclared step renders as its raw value -- visible and ugly, which is the point: a missing declaration must look missing.",
    "PLASMA_CLEAN": "플라즈마 세정",
    "BONDING": "본딩",
    "MOLDING": "몰딩",
    "POST_BOND_QUEUE": "본딩 후 대기",
    "MI_THICKNESS": "두께 계측",
